  {
   "id": "NS-188",
   "group": "prose",
   "kind": "positive",
   "text": "The prosecution examined twelve witnesses in support of the charge. the informant stated that on 12.07.2026 at about 10.30 PM the accused came to his shop and demanded Rs. 5,000/- failing which he threatened to burn it down. The testimony was corroborated by a neighbour, who reached the spot immediately. The defence pleaded false implication, but no material was produced to support the plea.",
   "expressions": [
    "12.07.2026",
    "10.30",
    "5,000"
   ],
   "note": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "NS-189",
   "group": "prose",
   "kind": "positive",
   "text": "Heard learned counsel for the appellant and the learned Public Prosecutor for the State. The trial court convicted the appellant under Section 302 IPC and sentenced him to life imprisonment. On a careful reappraisal of the evidence this Court finds that the ocular version is consistent with the medical evidence, and no ground for interference is made out in the appeal.",
   "expressions": [
    "302"
   ],
   "note": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "NS-190",
   "group": "prose",
   "kind": "positive",
   "text": "The seizure list, marked as Ext. P-3, records the recovery of one knife from beneath the bed of the accused in the presence of two independent witnesses. Both witnesses supported the prosecution on this point and nothing in their cross-examination shakes their testimony. The learned trial court rightly relied upon it while holding the accused guilty of the offence.",
   "expressions": [
    "3"
   ],
   "note": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "NS-191",
   "group": "prose",
   "kind": "positive",
   "text": "The application under Section 439 CrPC for bail was moved on 18.06.2025 and was opposed by the State on the ground that the accused is a habitual offender with three prior cases registered against him. Having considered the rival submissions and the period of custody undergone, this Court is inclined to grant bail on stringent conditions to be complied with by the petitioner.",
   "expressions": [
    "439",
    "18.06.2025"
   ],
   "note": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "NS-192",
   "group": "prose",
   "kind": "positive",
   "text": "The learned counsel submitted that the impugned order suffers from non-application of mind and that the reasons recorded are perfunctory. Reliance was placed on several decisions of the Supreme Court. However, none of those decisions is applicable to the peculiar facts of the case at hand, and the argument is therefore rejected without any further discussion.",
   "expressions": [],
   "note": ""
  }
 ]
